-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The XRCC1 -77T-&#x0003e;C variant: haplotypes, breast cancer risk, response to radiotherapy and the cellular response to DNA damage</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>2006</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>2469</fpage><lpage>2474</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Carcinogenesis||27|2469||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16829685</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cetintas</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozkan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurt</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Saran</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tasdelen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Tolunay</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Topal</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Engin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors influencing cosmetic results after breast conserving management (Turkish experience)</article-title><source>Breast</source><year>2002</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Breast||11|72||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14965649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang-Claude</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Popanda</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>XL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kropp</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Helmbold</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>von Fournier</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Haase</surname><given-n